    "text": "To determine how many pillows Teddy can make, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the amount of fluffy foam material used per pillow:**\n   Teddy uses 3 less than 5 pounds of fluffy foam material to make each pillow. Therefore, the amount of material used per pillow is:\n   \\[\n   5 - 3 = 2 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Convert the total amount of fluffy foam material from tons to pounds:**\n   Since 1 ton is equal to 2000 pounds, we convert 3 tons to pounds:\n   \\[\n   3 \\text{ tons} \\times 2000 \\text{ pounds/ton} = 6000 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine how many pillows can be made with the total amount of fluffy foam material:**\n   To find out how many pillows can be made, we divide the total amount of fluffy foam material by the amount used per pillow:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{6000 \\text{ pounds}}{2 \\text{ pounds/pillow}} = 3000 \\text{ pillows}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the number of pillows Teddy can make is \\(\\boxed{3000}\\).",
